{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "The Vision and Scarlet Witch — Mono-Red Spellslinger Voltron",
  "format": "commander",
  "description": "Research: research/decisions.md · pilot notes: research/gameplan.md.\n\n**Gameplan:** every spell you cast refunds {R} and puts a +1/+1 counter on a 3/3 flier. So the\ndeck is built out of one-mana cantrips that replace themselves (Crash Through, Expedite, Crimson\nWisps, Might of the Meek…) — each one is mana-neutral, draws a card, grows the commander and\nfires every burn trigger on the board (Guttersnipe, Firebrand Archer, Kessig Flamebreather,\nCoruscation Mage, Thermo-Alchemist, Fiery Inscription, Longshot). Bank the surplus: Leyline\nTyrant, Electro and Ashling stop red mana from emptying, so rituals and refunds pile up across\nturns and Braid of Fire becomes a growing deposit. Spend the bank on a storm turn — Grapeshot,\nAetherflux Reservoir, Crackle with Power — or on a suited-up commander swing with Embercleave and\nBulk Up, and Kediss turns one connected hit into damage to every opponent.\n\n**Protection is a role, not a card.** Hexproof (Champion's Helm, Swiftfoot Boots), protection\nfrom four colours (Commander's Plate), indestructible (Mithril Coat, Tyrite Sanctum), redirects\n(Deflecting Swat, Bolt Bend), uncounterable (Hexing Squelcher, Cavern of Souls), no spells on\nyour turn (Conqueror's Flail), and The Ozolith so the counters survive a death. Nothing here\ncovers edicts and exile wraths — the answer to those is a cheap recast plus the Ozolith bank.",
